  "body": "Consider this testcase:\n\n```\n<script onload=\"alert('hey')\">function f()</script>\n```\n\nShould there be an alert?  Per spec, I think there should be:\n1. Start at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#scriptEndTag\n2. Land in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#prepare-a-script which goes through the various steps and eventually lands in step 20, which will go to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#execute-the-script-block\n3. Step 8 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#execute-the-script-block sees the script type is \"classic\" but not from an external file, so queues a task to fire a simple event named \"load\" at the script element.\n\nI don't see such an event in Gecko, Blink, or WebKit nightly.  I do see one in Edge and IE11...  So maybe the other UAs just need to update to follow the spec here.\n",
